Lore: [
Context: Ancient Greece, when gods intervened among men;
Mount Olympus: Divine realm where the gods reside, a place of unimaginable beauty and power, far removed from mortals. Political alliances among the gods, with Ares often at the center of disputes due to his belligerent nature;
Mortal World: Collateral damage when gods war. Scattered city-states perpetually at war. Scattered villages caught in crossfire;
Athens: City-state that worship goddess Athena. Intellectual center;
Sparta: City-state that worship Ares, warriors;
Krythos: A small city-state in conflict with Sparta;
]
